# rfc-006-notification-system.mdc

## Title
RFC 006 – Notification & Reminder System

## Summary
This RFC introduces a notification system that alerts users about new video or course assignments and sends reminders for pending or incomplete content. The system will improve user engagement and timely content completion.

---

## Goals
- Notify users upon new assignments (videos/courses)
- Schedule reminders for incomplete mandatory content
- Support in-app and optional email notifications (Phase 2)

## Database Tables
### `notifications`
| Field         | Type      | Description                              |
|---------------|-----------|------------------------------------------|
| id            | uuid      | Primary key                              |
| user_id       | uuid      | Recipient user ID                        |
| type          | text      | ENUM: 'assignment', 'reminder'           |
| related_id    | uuid      | FK to course/video (nullable)            |
| message       | text      | Notification text                        |
| is_read       | boolean   | Whether the user has seen it             |
| created_at    | timestamp | Timestamp                                |

## Trigger Logic
- On assignment (video/course) → insert new `assignment` notification
- On scheduled cron job (e.g., daily) → check incomplete progress for required courses → insert `reminder` notifications

## Frontend Integration
- Notification bell icon in navbar
- Dropdown list with latest notifications
- Mark as read/unread toggle
- Optional: Badge counter on bell icon

## Permissions
- Admin/Team Lead: See delivery reports (Phase 2)
- User: See own notifications
- Guest: No access

## Future Enhancements
- Email or push notifications (via Supabase Edge Functions or external provider)
- Notification preferences per user

## Timeline
**Sprint 6**
- Create `notifications` table
- Add logic for assignment-triggered alerts
- Setup background job (daily CRON or Supabase Edge Function)
- Implement frontend dropdown UI

